00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:56.300
Yamamoto-san, are you still
drawing manga, like always?

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.920
What? Well, I'm scraping along.

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:01.420
You really don't change, 
do you, Yamamoto-san?

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:04.540
Even back in high school, you were 
completely dedicated to manga, right?

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:08.800
Well, at my age, 
I do wonder if it's all right.

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:11.440
Yeah, we are sort of old for that.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:14.070
Once you're over thirty, 
it's super-hard to get married.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:17.520
If you don't hurry up, face reality, 
and find a man soon...

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:22.150
Shut up! I'm doing this because I want to!

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:24.330
You got a problem with that?!

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.400
Don't you think they're horrible?

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:31.070
Why do they look down on otaku-y things?

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:34.090
No idea.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:39.320
The thing is, I am currently 
suffering great anguish.

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:42.710
This is the moment to elevate 
the social status of the 2D.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:44.970
I believe we should resolutely fight to...

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:52.330
<i>There's someone here who seems to be 
suffering greater anguish than I.</i>

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:57.360
Here, Kosuke-san. Please drink this.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:59.350
Thanks.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:01.950
Are you worried about something?

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:05.120
We'd be happy to give advice if you'd like.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.620
Now, you can say anything to us.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:08.740
Thanks.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.320
Yamamoto-senpai.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:14.980
Actually, yesterday, Yukimura-senpai 
and the others ran an experiment.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:18.750
A whole bunch of couples went 
on dates at the same time.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.240
My! How lovely!

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:23.700
I participated, too, with Aika.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:24.490
What?

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:28.020
And then I... I...

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.310
<i>Are you serious?</i>

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:33.560
I wondered, "Why am I the only one playing 
with a doll?! Isn't that creepy?!"

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:36.650
"Why am I the only one who 
doesn't have a 3D girlfriend?!"

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.400
Tsundere

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.400
Cute

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.400
Nice Figure

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.400
Kind

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.400
Pretty 2D Girl

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.400
Cute

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.400
Nice Figure

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.400
Doesn't Poop

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.400
Pretty
Costume

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.400
Pop Idol

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:39.400
After Yukimura-senpai gave me validation...

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.300
I thought I'd live my 
whole life loving Aika!

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:47.770
But! In the end, when I was with all 
of them, I was just a creepy guy!

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:51.530
Yes. Well, you are creepy, Torasuke.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:55.610
Falling in love with a thing like this... 
That really is disgusting.

00:05:56.170 --> 00:06:01.040
It's physically and psychologically impossible. 
Face reality. Live better.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:05.810
I wonder if people of sexual minorities have 
always had those things said to them, too?

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:11.140
Hey, have you heard of the Kinsey scale?

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:11.790
Huh?

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:15.800
A biologist named Kinsey 
came up with the concept.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:23.070
<b>Homosexual People</b>

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:23.070
<b>Heterosexual People</b>

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:21.210
It's impossible to separate people cleanly 
into heterosexual and heterosexual groups.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.310
There are those who exist in-between.

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:27.320
Exclusively
Heterosexual

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:27.320
Predominantly
heterosexual,
only incidentally
homosexual

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:27.320
Predominantly
heterosexual,
but more than
incidentally
homosexual

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:27.320
Equally
heterosexual
and
homosexual

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:27.320
Predominantly
homosexual,
but more than
incidentally
heterosexual

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:27.320
Predominantly
homosexual,
only
incidentally
heterosexual

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:27.320
Exclusively
Homosexual

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:27.310
It's a way of thinking which 
includes a seven layer gradation.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:32.720
It's true there are bisexuals 
who like both men and women.

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:34.890
And some people are heterosexual,

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:38.580
<b>ba-dump</b>

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:38.580
but occasionally someone of the same 
gender makes their heart skip a beat.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:43.100
According to a recent survey done 
in England using the Kinsey scale,

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:48.390
among young people, 46% of people 
were exclusively heterosexual.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.470
Exclusively Heterosexual

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.470
Exclusively Homosexual

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:50.460
Forty-six percent?!

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:52.270
That's less than half!

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:53.720
That means...

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:58.970
over half of the young people in 
England have the potential for BL?

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:02.910
Apparently, the results were 
different in older people,

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:05.810
but the number of people with, at least, 
a trace of homosexuality

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:07.230
was greater than they'd expected.

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:09.560
That gives me tremendous hope!

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:12.740
Yeah, it is hope for those 
in the sexual minority.

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:15.620
I wonder how love for 2D would fare.

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:17.620
That's it!

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.900
Those who love 2D and those who love 3D

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:23.500
Love for 2D

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:23.490
should also be broken down into a 
gradation like the Kinsey scale!

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:23.500
Love for 3D

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:28.260
People in this world who can't get 
worked up over an illustration...

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:31.630
and people who've gotten married, 
but still stay otaku!

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:35.630
There are even guys with aggravated cases 
who can't get off to a pic of real people!

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:43.400
<b>People Who
Love 3D</b>

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:43.400
<b>People Who Can
Love Either</b>

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:43.400
<b>People Who
Love 2D</b>

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:39.470
If I look into the percentages 
in each position,

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:44.120
there might be a lot of people with 
at least a little love of the 2D!

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:46.390
That's right, Kosuke-san!

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:48.260
After all, I myself am like that.

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:51.070
I'm always thinking only 
of manga characters.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.540
But there are people who make fun of that,

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.030
so even I thought I must be odd.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:02.290
But E* from F*llm*tal or Ey*s from Sp*ral... 
I was really in love with them!

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:05.830
Really falling in love with characters 
like that once or twice...

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:07.880
I'm sure there must be lots 
of people who have done that!

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.890
Let's look into it.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:19.520
Kosuke-san, you make this "2D Lover" test,

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:22.890
and I'll create a manga and 
collect data from my readers.

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:28.900
If were talking about games, 
I like Aika the most, too.

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:35.170
Torasuke, you may be a 
creepy, 2D-loving man,

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:39.150
but I'm sure we're not alone.

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:42.300
You go out and prove it.

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:43.810
I'll leave it to you.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:46.600
Sounds like fun.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:48.540
I'll do it.

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:52.110
This world is overflowing with 2D love...

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:55.100
Loving 2D is nothing strange...

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:57.160
I'll prove it!

00:08:57.410 --> 00:09:00.520
I am a man who lives by love! 
Inukai Kosuke!

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:04.320
I will become the hope of 
everyone who loves 2D!

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:08.950
I'm gonna verify the percentage 
of 2D lovers in the world!

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:10.060
Let's do it!

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:12.930
We will bring hope to the 2D!

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:14.330
I'll be counting on you!

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:20.340
Oh, I'm so glad.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:23.980
Kosuke-san has completely cheered up,

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.710
and I found material for my manga.

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.230
I'm looking forward to the research!

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:30.970
What will the results be?

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:31.710
Arika.

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:36.090
Don't do anything strange to Torasuke.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:40.240
What do you mean by "strange"? 
Ena, you have such a dirty mind!

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:42.960
Or could this be jealousy? Are you jealous?

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:47.990
No. It's because I know many 
of your previous offenses.

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:53.990
Honestly. I won't do anything. 
There's no need to warn me like this.

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:57.320
Is Kosuke-san that to you?

00:09:57.650 --> 00:09:59.600
Yes. Is there a problem with that?

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:10.340
She really is adorable, that Ena.

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:11.620
But, you know...

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:15.900
there is nothing which does not change.

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:19.680
You've worked hard today, Himuro-senpai.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.130
Thank you.

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:25.070
Being a teaching assistant 
looks like difficult work.

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:28.760
I wonder if I'll be able to manage 
like you do next year, Himuro-senpai.

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:30.940
O-Oh, right. Kanade-chan?

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:32.890
Yes?

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:37.290
I love you.

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:46.040
Science Fell in Love,
So I Tried to Prove It [<b>r=1-sinθ</b>]

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:48.870
Himuro-senpai?

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:54.670
Huh? Um... Th-This is a joke, right?

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:58.580
Himuro-senpai, you have 
Yukimura-senpai, don't you?

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:01.210
Plus, we're both women, so...

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:03.310
Honestly, you're being silly, Himuro-senpai.

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:05.060
No! Please listen!

