13. B is a person who easily gains the praise of others.</b>

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:55.910
Huh? You're asking if I'm 
gonna let you read them?

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:58.470
Rewind, pause, and read, bear.

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:01.350
And it isn't my problem if people 
aren't recording this, bear.

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:03.660
Watch it again via streaming, bear!

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:07.580
W-Wait! Just wait, please, 
for all kinds of reasons!

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:10.710
First, this Rubin's love thingy.

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:15.430
Isn't it exactly that "definition of love" 
you all have been researching to find?

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:18.120
Oh, well, yes it is, but...

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:23.380
as I've said before, it's impossible to 
arrive at an absolute definition of love.

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:25.010
This scale is the same.

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:29.060
Even matching it completely doesn't mean 
that you can definitively state that it's love.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:34.130
In the end, this is no more than one standard, 
like those we were trying to create.

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:39.020
Then, doesn't that mean you can't 
determine that you love me either?

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:42.480
What does it hurt?

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:44.530
It's basically something you can 
decide for yourself anyway!

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:46.890
Then we didn't need to talk 
about Rubin at all, did we?

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:48.570
I-In any case,

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:50.760
I love you, Kanade-chan.

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:53.370
Just as stated in Rubin's 
scale of linking number 11,

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:56.680
you are one of the most 
likable people I know!

00:12:56.670 --> 00:13:02.590
<b>11. When I am with A, I can pass the time just
\h\h\h\h\h\hlooking at them.
 12. I enjoy being confided in by A.
 13. It is hard for me when A and I don't get along.</b>

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:58.440
And love scale number 13,

00:12:56.710 --> 00:13:02.590
▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬

00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:02.330
"It is hard for me when you and I don't 
get along" rings really true for me.

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:04.250
Number 5, "I feel very possessive toward A,"

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:04.840
<b>2. I trust A completely.
 3. I find it easy to ignore A's faults.
 4. I would do almost anything for A.
 5. I feel very possessive toward A.
 6. If I could never be with A, I would feel miserable.
 7. When I am lonely, my first thought is to seek A out.
 8. One of my primary concerns is A's happiness.</b>

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:04.840
▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:06.670
and number 8, "One of my primary 
concerns is A's happiness,"

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:08.180
<b>5. I feel very possessive toward A.
 6. If I could never be with A, I would feel miserable.
 7. When I am lonely, my first thought is to seek A out.
 8. One of my primary concerns is A's happiness.
 9. I would forgive A for anything.
 10. I feel responsible for A's well being.
 11. When I am with A, I can pass the time just looking at them.</b>

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:08.180
▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:08.180
▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬

00:13:06.670 --> 00:13:08.190
I feel that way a little bit, too!

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:11.050
<i>Wait, wait, wait! 
What is this person saying?!</i>

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:13.360
That's why... um...

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:17.110
like in number 1, when you're feeling 
badly, I want to cheer you up.

00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:20.350
If you're feeling worried or anxious, 
I'd listen to anything you had to say.

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:24.060
Of course, if you don't want to talk 
about it, that's all right, too.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:28.580
I was wondering why you suddenly 
started saying you loved me.

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:34.040
I don't want to pry. 
It's just that I love you, Kanade-chan.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:38.580
That's why, no matter what happens, 
I want to be an ally to you.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:40.840
Oh, what am I saying?

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:42.830
I'm being weird, right?

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:47.320
<i>I see. She's worried about me.</i>

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:51.460
<i>No, no. Normally, you don't start 
this stuff with "I love you," right?</i>

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:54.400
<i>Why'd she talk about Rubin's love scale?!</i>

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:55.720
<i>She's way too panicked!</i>

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:57.030
I-I'm sorry!

00:13:57.030 --> 00:14:00.080
If you don't like this, or if it's none of 
my business, just forget it, all right?

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:02.870
<i>To be trying so awkwardly, so desperately...</i>

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:05.990
<i>for the sake of someone like me...</i>

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:07.910
Kanade-chan?

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:12.310
I love you, too!

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:15.120
I love you, Himuro-senpai! 
I love you so much!

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:18.160
Kanade-chan.

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:23.410
I'm so happy. I love you, too, 
Kanade-chan. I love you so much.

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:25.260
I love you more!

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:29.630
Himuro-senpai.

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:31.470
I'm scared.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:36.530
Back in high school, my love failed. 
I keep thinking it'll turn out that way again.

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:38.510
What happened?

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:41.520
I have heard what you have to say.

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:46.650
That is extremely valuable 
information for our research.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:49.640
Now, speak. Tell us of your 1 Kanade-love.

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:52.240
You will tell us and leave nothing out!

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:54.280
<b>Force of Impact</b>

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:57.550
Again, what's with your 
complete lack of delicacy?

00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:04.930
Now, Kanade-chan, will you 
tell us what happened?

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:07.210
Whatever you feel able 
to speak about is fine.

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:11.770
My family has a martial arts dojo.

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:15.470
I've received training ever 
since I was little.

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:17.180
<b>Honed Through a Hundred Battles</b>

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:17.180
<b>Goddess
of Light
and
Warriors</b>

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:17.180
<b>Katori
Okami,
God of
Warriors</b>

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:17.180
<b>Takemikazuchi,
God of
Thunder
and Swords</b>

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:16.380
Ha!

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:19.540
Hup!

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:23.190
Grandpa, why do we do martial arts?

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:25.080
Out in the world,

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:30.320
unfortunately, there are many reprehensible 
scoundrels who prowl after women's bodies.

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:33.320
Even if you are attacked 
by one of those people,

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:38.070
I know that the martial arts you've ingrained 
in your body will keep you safe, Koto-chan.

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:41.440
Until one day, when someone you 
think will make you happy,

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:44.910
someone you truly love, appears.

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:52.260
Someone like that appeared before 
me when I was in high school.

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:55.230
Takahashi Keisuke, my teacher.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:16:01.090
I... I'm in love with you, Sensei.

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.730
I appreciate your feelings, but...

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:11.000
you're a student, and I'm your teacher.

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:14.710
We... can't have that kind of relationship.

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:17.110
All I can do...

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:19.980
is teach you math.

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:21.750
If that's enough, then...

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:27.700
Then, teach me properly, please. 
I'll study really hard!

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:33.780
After that day, 
Sensei taught math just for me.

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:36.140
Day after day...

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:39.370
I just wanted to be with him.

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:42.880
I wanted to love the same things he loved.

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:45.650
The more time we spent together,

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:48.640
the more I loved him, in direct proportion.

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:49.900
[1] 1st Choice School, Evaluation
Combined test results upon which this evaluation was made
1st Choice
Saitama University, Science Department
Combined Score: <b>C</b>

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:52.780
Your scores have really 
improved, Kanade-kun.

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:56.110
With these, you might really be able 
to aim for Saitama University.

00:16:56.850 --> 00:16:58.910
Um, Sensei...

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:02.660
If I manage to get a B 
on the next mock exam...

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:05.780
will you go on a date with me? Just once?

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:08.800
Well...

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:12.640
if it's just the two of us going 
somewhere, then all right.

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:17.300
Every day sparkled brightly.

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:20.060
Combined Score: <b>B</b>

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:22.300
If it were for his sake, 
I felt like I could do anything.

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:36.330
That's cold!

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:37.900
Here, Sensei!

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:39.820
Thank you.

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:41.780
Oh. I'll pay for it.

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:45.840
No. I'd like to treat you sometimes, too.

00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:49.750
I can't allow that. W-Wait, Kanade-kun!

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:50.850
Don't wanna!

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:57.590
<i>Grandpa, I finally understand!</i>

00:17:57.590 --> 00:18:01.070
Until one day, when someone you 
think will make you happy,

00:18:01.070 --> 00:18:04.590
someone you truly love, appears.

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:08.350
<i>What you meant was someone like this, right?</i>

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:14.530
<i>I know that the martial arts 
you've ingrained in your body...</i>

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:17.990
<i>will keep you safe, Koto-chan.</i>

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:19.240
<i>...safe.</i>

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:20.710
<i>...safe.</i>

00:18:21.110 --> 00:18:22.120
<i>...safe.</i>

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:30.390
I used a shoulder throw 
on the person I loved

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:32.620
and slammed him onto the pavement!

00:18:33.350 --> 00:18:34.720
<i>How can I put this...</i>

00:18:35.060 --> 00:18:37.500
<i>It's more... something 
than I supposed, but...</i>

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:40.390
<i>Well, that... would be traumatic.</i>

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:43.830
Sensei, I'm so sorry!

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:44.810
Excuse me.

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:46.020
I'm a doctor.

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:48.350
He's unconscious.

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:50.960
It's possible he has a concussion, 
so please don't move him.

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:53.700
He may have broken a bone 
in his shoulder, too.

00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:55.400
Someone call 119!

00:18:55.770 --> 00:18:57.700
Huh? What? Is someone hurt?

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.540
They said they're calling an ambulance.

00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:03.020
That was amazing. 
That girl just threw a man.

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:05.000
And he got seriously injured 
from it? That's crazy!

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:06.910
Was the man violent toward her or something?

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:09.180
It didn't seem like that kind 
of atmosphere between them.

00:19:09.180 --> 00:19:11.150
She's strong. Like a gorilla woman.

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:14.420
Looks like trouble. That girl isn't normal.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:18.480
It's because I was weird 
and did martial arts...

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:22.130
because I wasn't normal, 
those things happened.

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:25.650
I'm happy just being a normal girl...

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:28.320
to live normally, like everyone else.

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:30.880
I just want to have a normal romance.

00:19:30.880 --> 00:19:31.840
And yet...

00:19:32.430 --> 00:19:34.680
I wanted to make sure this 
date wouldn't fail...

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:37.200
so I took one step forward 
and tried really hard.

00:19:38.180 --> 00:19:39.700
But, just as I thought, it didn't work.

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:41.650
Why is that?

00:19:41.650 --> 00:19:44.310
Why can't I be normal?

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:46.830
I wonder if it just isn't possible for me.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:48.900
I don't think that's true.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:50.450
Kanade-chan, you're—

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:51.780
Kanade.

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:53.830
What is the definition of "normal"?

00:19:54.830 --> 00:20:00.530
I've thought this for a long time. 
You use the word "normal" quite often.

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:03.340
It's even possible to see that you 
use it as a creed to live by.

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:06.360
Let's do something normal!

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:09.670
We need to do normal girl 
stuff, every once in a while.

00:20:09.670 --> 00:20:12.350
Just being here, like normal, is the best.

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:14.780
What is this "normal" you speak of?

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:18.090
Is "everyone else" all of humanity? 
Japanese society?

00:20:18.090 --> 00:20:20.720
What percentage shares the same traits?

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:20.740
Can't be normal
20%?

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:20.740
Normal
80%?

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:20.740
Fig. 1.1: Proportions(?) Present in All of Humanity(?)

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:25.620
<b>Normal Set</b>

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:23.510
To live obsessed with the idea of "normal"

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:25.620
means to live without definite 
intentions and rules.

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:28.690
You simply synchronize 
with the "normal set,"

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:30.990
and continue to follow that 
group with blind obedience.

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:34.170
And you yourself will be an 
empty set filled with nothing.

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:36.440
That is a truly stupid way to live.

00:20:37.230 --> 00:20:40.460
Yukimura-kun! That's going too far!

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:42.640
It isn't you who should be getting angry.

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:45.400
If you have a counter-argument, 
then tell me, Kanade.

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:47.020
Do it intelligently.

00:20:53.860 --> 00:20:56.660
What... is so wrong about it?

00:20:58.160 --> 00:20:59.950
Making yourself empty...

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:02.980
To live adapting to the people 
around you... Is that wrong?

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:04.900
Everyone does that, don't they?

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:08.390
Being like you, Yukimura-senpai, 
always overflowing with confidence...

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:10.440
always true to your own convictions...

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:13.350
always being stared at by the people 
around you, like you're a weirdo...

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:14.800
like they're sick of you...

00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:17.680
and still not wavering, living calmly.

00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:21.050
Not everyone is like you, Senpai!

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:24.330
I don't want to show people who I really am!

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:26.420
I don't want to cause trouble 
for the people around me,

00:21:26.420 --> 00:21:27.970
and having people stare at me...

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:30.560
being embarrassed... I don't want that!

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:34.610
That's why I read the 
room and kill who I am!

00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:36.370
I blend into my surroundings!

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:38.880
I will live normally, without making waves!

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:40.930
What's so wrong about that?!

00:21:50.550 --> 00:21:52.610
If that's what you want to do,

00:21:52.610 --> 00:21:54.460
then spend your whole life living that way.

